    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148-a10">

                <pb facs="0398" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg280"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thurston to Mr. Bates.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">H.
                                M. S. Miranda</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Apia,
                            Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1886-09-05"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September</hi> 5,
                    1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, the receipt of your letter of the 2d of September, inclosing copy of a
                    letter which you have addressed to Mr. Travers, the German commissioner.</p>
                <p>I concur with you in thinking that it would have been of advantage if in certain
                    respects the commissioners had been able to conduct their inquiries in
                    concert.</p>
                <pb facs="0399" n="281" xml:id="pg281"/>
                <p>Allow me to take this opportunity of thanking you for the assistance and cordial
                    co-operation which you have accorded me in the performance of my duties at
                    Samoa.</p>
                <p>I have etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Thurston.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
